  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through next Wednesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: \n\nHigh Pressure remains in place this afternoon will keep Nevada \ndry through Friday. Temperatures look to warm into the upper 40s \nto upper 50s for highs, with light afternoon west to SW winds of 5\nto 15 MPH. Saturday morning an upper trough looks to pass through\nthe Pacific NW, Models are still keeping the bulk of this system \nto the north, precipitation chances have shifted a bit father \nsouth. Models now show precipitation reaching the I-80 corridor, \nwith a 10% to 20% chance for isolated showers, further north along\nthe ID/OR border chances rise to 20% to 40% for isolated to \nscattered showers. Snow levels will be rather high with this \nsystem at about 6500 feet, which will keep any snow from roadways \nwith the exception of NV 225 between Wildhorse Res. and Mountain \nCity, with lower elevations seeing rainfall. Amounts will be light\nwith up to a 0.10\u201d of rain, and 1\u201d to 4\u201d of snow for the mountain\npeaks along and north of I-80. Sunday will be a quiet day as a \nfast moving shortwave ridge follows in the wake of the trough. \nMonday, Tuesday and into Wednesday models still show a series of \nPacific trough take aim at the west, which will bring several \nrounds of widespread valley rain and mountain snow chances back to\nthe Great basin. Temperatures for now look to hold in the mid 40s\nto mid 50s for highs, and with lows holding in the mid 20s to mid\n30s. Models are keeping snow levels above 6000 feet for northern \nNevada, with central NV seeing snow levels near 7000 feet for now,\nbut recent models runs have been trending lower, but as models\nhave shown a cold bias for this time frame, will keep snow levels\nas is. So will go with a mix of valley rain mountain snow for the\nend of the week, as for amounts it is too soon to tell if amounts\nwill be significant with the first few systems, as totals look to\nrun between 0.05\u201d up to 0.35\u201d of liquid, with up to 3\u201d to 6\u201d of \nnew snow for the high peaks. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \n \nThere is high confidence in quiet weather pattern lasting through\nFriday of this week with high pressure dominating.\n\nThere is medium confidence in a quick moving upper trough passing\nthrough the Pacific NW bringing a low 10% to 40% chance of \nisolated to scattered showers for northern Nevada Saturday.\n\nThere is medium confidence in a pattern change beginning for the \nweekend, and getting under way for the start of next week, but low\nconfidence in timing and amounts for precipitation Monday through\nWednesday of next week.",
